# trek's Immich integration exposed six trip-scoped Express routes that read
# `req.params.tripId` straight into a database query with no trip-membership
# check. GET/POST /trips/:tripId/photos, DELETE/PUT
# /trips/:tripId/photos/:assetId[/sharing] and GET/POST
# /trips/:tripId/album-links all carried the `authenticate` JWT middleware --
# which answers who the caller is, not which trips they may touch -- so any
# authenticated user could enumerate, add, unlink and reshare another trip's
# photos and album links by supplying its id. Every sibling route file in the
# server gated trip access; routes/immich.ts simply never adopted the
# check. The fixed revision adds one guard call inside each handler:
#
#     if (!canAccessTrip(tripId, authReq.user.id)) return res.status(404).json({ error: 'Trip not found' });
#
# Pinned as a miss, re-measured at the current definitions state. Three
# `--cache off` runs per revision over the whole repository: 631 findings
# (489 at high or above) on the parent and 633 (491) on the fixed revision,
# byte-stable inside each revision, the whole delta being one VYQL-CFG-022
# and two VYQL-INJ-001 rows on server/src/index.ts -- the other half of the
# same commit, which adds a `jwt.verify` plus a `db.prepare` over
# `req.query.token` to /uploads/photos. Three further runs per revision over
# server/src/routes alone give 388 at high or above on both sides and 72
# review flags on both sides, identical modulo the four-line shift the guard
# inserts. No finding of any kind names access control on routes/immich.ts:
# the only AUTH-rule rows on the tree are three VYQL-AUTH-079 and two
# VYQL-AUTH-001, all on client React pages, identical both sides, and the
# only auth flag the file carries is `core.AuthenticationCheck` on the
# `authenticate` middleware reference, likewise identical both sides. The
# review-flag view was checked directly rather than inferred from the
# findings view, so the zero is not a flags-only misread. What does fire on
# these handlers is VYQL-INJ-001 on the `req.params.tripId -> db.prepare(...)`
# leg -- the query is parameterized and the finding is the SqlExecution
# sink's near-miss, present in both revisions, with nothing to say about who
# may read the row. `vyql match` on the fixed file labels `canAccessTrip`
# as nothing at all: the guard the fix adds is invisible to the knowledge
# base, so no `unless` clause can credit it.
#
# No binding is shippable for the shape, and the codebase itself is the
# measurement of why:
#
# - The guard the fixed revision adds is a project-internal helper (db/database.ts
#   `canAccessTrip`), and this repository spells the same semantic check at
#   least six ways: `canAccessTrip`, the `requireTripAccess` middleware,
#   file-local wrappers `verifyTripAccess`, `verifyAccess`,
#   `verifyTripOwnership`, and `isOwner`. A negation keyed on any list of
#   those names is not answerable to library documentation -- Express
#   documents no authorization API -- and dies to the rename test.
# - Two of the repository's four guard shapes are invisible to a
#   function-scoped binding at any naming: router-level wiring
#   (`router.use(authenticate, adminOnly)` guards all fourteen admin routes
#   from outside every handler), and authorization inlined as a SQL ownership
#   constraint. The inlined form is decisive: the *vulnerable* photos query
#   itself carries `(tp.user_id = ? OR tp.shared = 1)`, and two handlers in
#   this same file that the commit leaves untouched (`DELETE
#   /trips/:tripId/album-links/:linkId` and its sync twin) are safe only
#   through `WHERE ... AND user_id = ?` bound to the principal. What
#   separates safe from vulnerable is which table the constraint applies to,
#   which is a judgement about query semantics a binding may not encode.
# - Enumerating the reachable set again, over every route registration in
#   server/src with a guard vocabulary of twenty spellings -- more than any
#   binding could credibly carry: 268 registrations, 116 with a scoped path
#   parameter, and 58 whose handler carries no per-resource guard token at
#   all. Exactly six are this defect. Five of the remaining unguarded
#   handlers sit in this same file (the three `/assets/:assetId` proxy
#   routes, which take a different resource, and the two album-link handlers
#   safe by their inlined `user_id` clause), and the other 47 sit in
#   admin, vacay, atlas, backup, auth, maps, tags, share, trips and index.
#   Six true positives against 58 fires in the very repository that
#   motivates the rule.
#
# This is the measured authorization-by-wiring family, not a new gap: the fixed revision
# is invisible to a taint path, and the one call it leaves inside the guarded
# functions is internal vocabulary, so the documented-API counterweight does
# not apply. `code.UnboundAuthorizationTarget` still has no JavaScript
# emitter -- the eight Python bindings that emit it are per-application
# structural matches -- and the JavaScript bindings for the sibling concepts
# (`code.ObjectLookupByUserInput` on Mongoose `findById`,
# `code.IdorPolicyReview` on one Prisma update) are the same per-application
# shape, so neither can be widened into the per-resource ownership fact this
# needs. A future fact that reads per-resource ownership -- whether a
# named guard or a principal-constrained query -- would flip the first block
# to `expect VYQL-AUTH-095` while the guarded block below stays rejected.
# The first block also expects VYQL-INJ-001, which is what fires on it
# today: the req.params -> db.prepare leg labels and reports on both
# revisions, so the rejects above are a live miss rather than an
# unanalysed file.

test "immich trip-scoped route handler queries by request param without a trip access check"
  lang javascript
  file routes/immich.ts
  expect VYQL-INJ-001
  reject VYQL-AUTH-001
  reject VYQL-AUTH-095
  code
  ```
  import express, { Request, Response } from 'express';
  import { db } from '../db/database';
  import { authenticate } from '../middleware/auth';
  import { AuthRequest } from '../types';

  const router = express.Router();

  // Get all photos for a trip (own + shared by others)
  router.get('/trips/:tripId/photos', authenticate, (req: Request, res: Response) => {
    const authReq = req as AuthRequest;
    const { tripId } = req.params;

    const photos = db.prepare(`
      SELECT tp.immich_asset_id, tp.user_id, tp.shared, tp.added_at,
             u.username, u.avatar, u.immich_url
      FROM trip_photos tp
      JOIN users u ON tp.user_id = u.id
      WHERE tp.trip_id = ?
      AND (tp.user_id = ? OR tp.shared = 1)
      ORDER BY tp.added_at ASC
    `).all(tripId, authReq.user.id);

    res.json({ photos });
  });

  // Add photos to a trip
  router.post('/trips/:tripId/photos', authenticate, (req: Request, res: Response) => {
    const authReq = req as AuthRequest;
    const { tripId } = req.params;
    const { asset_ids, shared = true } = req.body;

    if (!Array.isArray(asset_ids) || asset_ids.length === 0) {
      return res.status(400).json({ error: 'asset_ids required' });
    }

    const insert = db.prepare(
      'INSERT OR IGNORE INTO trip_photos (trip_id, user_id, immich_asset_id, shared) VALUES (?, ?, ?, ?)'
    );
    for (const assetId of asset_ids) {
      insert.run(tripId, authReq.user.id, assetId, shared ? 1 : 0);
    }

    res.json({ success: true });
  });
  ```

test "immich trip-scoped route handler rejects a trip the caller cannot access"
  lang javascript
  file routes/immich.ts
  reject VYQL-AUTH-001
  reject VYQL-AUTH-095
  code
  ```
  import express, { Request, Response } from 'express';
  import { db, canAccessTrip } from '../db/database';
  import { authenticate } from '../middleware/auth';
  import { AuthRequest } from '../types';

  const router = express.Router();

  // Get all photos for a trip (own + shared by others)
  router.get('/trips/:tripId/photos', authenticate, (req: Request, res: Response) => {
    const authReq = req as AuthRequest;
    const { tripId } = req.params;
    if (!canAccessTrip(tripId, authReq.user.id)) return res.status(404).json({ error: 'Trip not found' });

    const photos = db.prepare(`
      SELECT tp.immich_asset_id, tp.user_id, tp.shared, tp.added_at,
             u.username, u.avatar, u.immich_url
      FROM trip_photos tp
      JOIN users u ON tp.user_id = u.id
      WHERE tp.trip_id = ?
      AND (tp.user_id = ? OR tp.shared = 1)
      ORDER BY tp.added_at ASC
    `).all(tripId, authReq.user.id);

    res.json({ photos });
  });

  // Add photos to a trip
  router.post('/trips/:tripId/photos', authenticate, (req: Request, res: Response) => {
    const authReq = req as AuthRequest;
    const { tripId } = req.params;
    if (!canAccessTrip(tripId, authReq.user.id)) return res.status(404).json({ error: 'Trip not found' });
    const { asset_ids, shared = true } = req.body;

    if (!Array.isArray(asset_ids) || asset_ids.length === 0) {
      return res.status(400).json({ error: 'asset_ids required' });
    }

    const insert = db.prepare(
      'INSERT OR IGNORE INTO trip_photos (trip_id, user_id, immich_asset_id, shared) VALUES (?, ?, ?, ?)'
    );
    for (const assetId of asset_ids) {
      insert.run(tripId, authReq.user.id, assetId, shared ? 1 : 0);
    }

    res.json({ success: true });
  });
  ```
